  "problem": "Suppose that a matrix $D$ has characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )=(\\lambda +e)^{4}(\\lambda -\\pi )^{3}(\\lambda -1)^{5},$ the nullity of $(D+eI)^{3}$ equals $3,$ and the nullity of $(D+eI)^{4}$ equals $4.$ If a basis of ${R}^{12}$ consists of linearly independent generalized eigenvectors of $D,$ how many of these are generalized eigenvectors of rank $4$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-e?$",
